DA Boly RAARR</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=2015&lastnode_id=1983">Re: Part of the shaman epic - Killing the Black Dire</a> (0 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=211&lastnode_id=1983">Boilybut</a> on 2001-07-12 09:41:49</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>oops, seems i metioned the obstacle, but not the solution.  anyway, i suggest everyone who is going, to print out a map of lesserfay, or at least go to a site like everlore and just study it if you cant print.  look for one with locs and write down the loc of the brownie village, and the darkelf camp, as these are the most common dangers to travelers.  however, they also have wandering brownies now, which are very tough, so i suggest evryone go with sow, and with back up.  if you do run into a brownie tho, yer still pretty screwed, since they are sowed, and can wipe out a full party of lvl 40s.<br>
<br>
But there's hope!  you can avoid all of this (except the DE camp, but not many of us are kos to them anyway) simply by following "Boily's lesserfay system".  all i need is your credit card number.  just kiddin:<br>
<br>
ok first, get a bind on the other side of the zone in greater fey. you can bind right there and its totaly safe.  next, zone in and follow the wall to your LEFT.  heres the tricky part, some areas along the wall go up high and make you think you have come to a corner of the zone.  Dont be fooled!  this is how quite a few peeple got lost last time.  go over EVERY hill you come to, untill you cant, THAT will be the zone corner.  i have not been there in some time, but ill list the land marks (that i member) that you will see along the way once you begin along the LEFT wall:<br>
<br>
1) not too far off is the first zone corner, pretty empty here<br>
<br>
2) you'll come to the steamfont zone not too much farther.  it has a road leading out to a few houses that you can see from the wall, STAY AWAY FROM THEM<br>
<br>
3) after a jog you should see a large structure with stone wings out a ways from the wall.  this is shadowman land, about 6 to 8 of them. so unless you can kill these things easy, stay away from this as well.  you should be able to bypass it by keeping to the wall.<br>
<br>
4) after a bit longer you'll come to the next zone corner.  (i cant remember if the zone corner or the shadowmen come first, but they are kinda close together).<br>
<br>
5) after a while longer you'l come across the DE camp.  this camp is right near he bottum of a steap hill, so it is easy to just run ontop of it, especially with sow.  so if you are kos to DEs be carefull, get a loc of the camp beofre hand, and keep an eye out for it over every hill along this strech.  ALSO, not a good idea to try passing them along the wall. keep them at a safe distance and vnture out into the woods a bit, but dont lose sight of them or you could get lost.  after you pass them go back to he zone wall.<br>
<br>
6) after a short jog you wil see a camp out to yer left a little ways, these are bandits, not much to worry about, but a good land mark, it means yer close.  i forget there names, they are all female, its called the sister camp.<br>
<br>
7) not to much farther you will come across a ruins along the wall, they kinda look like druid circle stones.  this marks the zone to MM.  Your there!<br>
<br>
so you see, its quite easy.  one of my biggest problems in an unamiliar zone is that i think i might ave gone too far, but with these land marks you should be fine.  theres only one real danger and thats the DEs.<br>
<br>
just remember that the zone wall is your friend, he likes you, he wants you close, so stick to it and you might live, until you enter MM that is :)<br>
<br>
Da Boily RARR<br>
<br>
